`context/instructions/todo.md` is the contract for the centralized idea inbox.
Read it when `context/todo.yaml` is relevant: a `>todo` capture, or a request to
list or close an item.

## The inbox

`context/todo.yaml` is the idea inbox: very short objectives or ideas for future
analyses. It is **CLI-owned** — read it, and change it only through
`sdt context todo`, never by hand. One short idea per item.

The human-readable projection is `context/todo.md`, regenerated on every
mutation; the register stays the source of truth.

## Annotate only

`>todo` (and `sdt context todo add`) **only records** the idea. It never starts
an analysis, a plan, a task or any operation:

- **Never begin work from `>todo`.** Capture the line and stop.
- A capture is not a commitment: draining the inbox is a later, separate
  `>draft`/`>analysis`.
- Keep each item short — an objective or an idea, not a plan.

## The verbs

- `sdt context todo add "<text>" [--id <slug>] [--source <ref>]` — add one idea.
- `sdt context todo list` — show the items.
- `sdt context todo done <id>` — mark an item done (kept in the list).
- `sdt context todo remove <id>` — drop an item.

`>todo: <text>` is the agent trigger; a bullet list adds one item per line.

## Boundaries

- The inbox holds the *idea* only: the work type belongs to the analysis
  `categories`, the subject to `topics`, and the *how* to an instruction — none
  duplicates another.
- An item is register data, not a document kind or a lifecycle stage.
